<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79008" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράφᾰσις</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράφημι</span>) only in poet. forms <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραίφᾰσις</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάρφᾰσις</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>address,
				encouragement, consolation</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαθὴ δὲ παραίφασίς ἐστιν ἑταίρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.793
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραίφασιν εὗρεν ἐρώτων</span>
			<i>a way of calming</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				5.373.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>allurement, persuasion</i>, in the cestus of Aphrodite, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάρφασις, ἥ τ᾽ ἔκλεψε νόον πύκα περ
					φρονεόντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.217
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>deceitful speaking</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθρὰ πάρφασις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					8.32
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
